From 26e4dda0e74a79cbe6a80ae3e7f8500b155c4692 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niri-RDP rebase <niri-rdp@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] headless: pace redraws and frame callbacks on a fixed-phase
 vblank

The headless backend simulated vblank with a timer started a full refresh
interval after each render, so every frame lasted the interval plus the
client's and niri's render time. Redraws queued while that timer was
pending (WaitingForEstimatedVBlankAndQueued) also ran immediately and
restarted the timer, so continuous remote pointer motion kept it from ever
firing. Its callback was the only place headless surfaces got frame
callbacks: the redraw path's send_frame_callbacks() filters on the primary
scanout output, which headless rendering never records. Applications fell
back to the one-second fallback timer while the pointer moved.

render() now presents at the next refresh boundary from the frame clock and
waits in WaitingForVBlank, like a DRM page flip: later redraw requests only
set redraw_needed and run when the simulated vblank fires. That timer sends
frame callbacks to every surface on the virtual output each refresh, then
queues the pending redraw or animation frame. It returns quietly if the
output was removed or its state changed meanwhile.
